Wound events initialize an impact burst and, independently, a finite bleeding
reservoir with configurable rate, clotting/decay time and optional pressure pulse.
FluidFilm supplies a transported, mass-conserving mobile layer on surfaces,
while Porous handles separate saturation and anisotropic wicking. Rigid ground
surfaces use local 48x48 projected film patches instead of a giant texture atlas.

Wound coverage uses 16-bit mobile-depth and 16-bit retained-depth values,
packed into one GPU word per texel; the renderer reconstructs wetness, roughness,
color and thin-film normals from physical thickness. The old mark list is
bounded impact history, NOT a procedural stamp renderer.

A UV chart is only a parameterization: correct flow over a moving or curved
character requires the game to register its real triangle geometry and
subsequently provide deformed vertex positions/transforms as needed.
Physical-chart-edge detachment must be explicitly enabled: UV seams are
not real mesh edges. Full anatomical bullet injury, vascular pressure and
measured model-material constants are outside this baseline implementation.
No claim of quantitative physiological accuracy or fully validated 60FPS.
